@capability-en1998-1-evaluate
@oracle-en1998-1-compliance-independent
@comparison-numerical-v1
Feature: EN 1998 Annex A, B, F, pile and N2 formulas against independent references
  The Rust functions and the Python oracle (scipy, numpy, groundhog) compute the same values from the same inputs.

  Further specification assertions, asserted by the Rust unit tests of the crate and not by the platform adapters:
  - The chord rotation capacity follows from the member section: Given a rectangular member 0.30 m by 0.50 m with d = 0.45 m, L_V = 2.0 m, N = 300 kN, A_s1 = 18 cm2, A_s2 = 9 cm2, f_y = 500 MPa, f_c = 30 MPa and stirrups 2 x 10 mm at 0.10 m When the neutral axis at yield is solved by equilibrium with a bracketing root finder Then the closed-form xi_y equals the root to 1e-9 And theta_um by A.1 equals the printed expression to 1e-9 And theta_y by A.10b with the yield curvature of the fibre section equals the printed expression with the oracle's strip integration to 0.3 percent
  - The section moment-curvature gives yield and ultimate point: Given the same member with parabola-rectangle concrete up to the registry strength range and elastic perfectly plastic steel When the fibre section is integrated by the shared mechanics kernel and by the oracle's fine strip integration with brentq on the strain plane and on the first strain limit Then phi_y, M_y, phi_u and M_u agree to 0.3 percent, the yield curvature is the first of the tension steel at f_y/E_s and the extreme concrete at eps_c2, the ultimate curvature the first of eps_cu and the steel strain limit, and a strength above the registry range leaves theta_y to the cracked elastic curvature
  - Annex B has no depth reduction and Youd et al. has: Given a layer at 6 m with (N1)60 = 12, 20 % fines, a ground water table at 2 m, Ms = 6.5 and a_g S = 0.75 m/s2 When the cyclic stress ratio is computed by groundhog with r_d switched off Then the Annex B stress ratio equals it to 1e-9 And the Youd et al. stress ratio is smaller by r_d(6 m) = 0.9541
  - The Annex F surface is reached at the load factor found by a root finder: Given N = 0.3 MN, V = 0.05 MN, M = 0.08 MN m, B = 2 m, N_max = 1 MN, phi' = 35 degrees and a_g S = 0.25 g When the load factor on the surface is found with brentq Then the utilisation is its inverse to 1e-9 And the section limits for M = 0 and V = 0 equal the roots of the surface to 1e-9
  - The pile moments equal a boundary value solution on the Winkler bed: Given a pile 0.6 m in diameter, E = 30 GPa, k_h = 20 MN/m3, a head shear of 100 kN and a length of 40 m When the beam equation is solved with solve_bvp for a free and for a fixed head Then the maximum moment and the head deflection equal the closed forms to 1e-4
  - The N2 target displacement equals the fixed point of the equal-energy idealisation: Given a three-storey shear building with storey resistances When the first mode comes from a generalised eigenproblem and the idealisation is iterated Then Gamma, m*, d_y, V_y, T*, q_u and d_t* equal the Rust values to 1e-6
  - The cantilever mode shapes follow the roots of 1 + cos x cosh x: Given a uniform cantilever When the roots are found with brentq and the participation with quad Then beta_n L, the shape at mid height, the participation and the period ratio equal the Rust values
  - Table F.1 constants equal the target spec and stay unverified: Given the registry rows of the Annex F sand set When the constants are read through the Annex F surface Then e, f, k, beta and gamma equal the GE-06 values 0.92, 0.41, 0.39, 2.57 and 4.0 and every row is unverified
  - The layered soil profile equals a quadrature and groundhog: Given a three-layer profile with unit weights, velocities, blow counts and fines contents When the stresses are integrated with quad, the stress ratio comes from groundhog without depth reduction and v_s,30 from quad Then the stresses, F_L per layer, v_s,30 and the site period equal the Rust values to 1e-9
  - The N2 roof capacity follows the weakest storey mechanism: Given the three-storey shear building with a chord rotation capacity of 0.03 rad in a 3.2 m storey When the weakest storey and its plateau drift come from the generalised eigenproblem Then the roof target, the roof capacity and the required chord rotation equal the Rust values to 1e-6
  - An accelerogram set is accepted by count and mean spectrum: Given three records and their spectra over the period range When the mean spectrum over the elastic spectrum is formed with numpy Then the lowest ratio equals the Rust value and the set needs at least three records
  - The diaphragm resistance equals a quadrature of the shear diagram: Given a diaphragm 24 m by 16 m with t = 0.20 m, tau_Rd = 1.0 MPa, openings of 2.4 m, a chord of 0.01 m2 at 435 MPa and a storey force of 500 kN with gamma_d = 1.3 When the shear diagram V(x) = F_d (1/2 - x/L) is integrated with quad Then F_d, V_Ed, V_Rd, the required thickness, the shear flow, the chord force at mid span and at the quarter point, N_Rd and the required chord area equal the Rust values
  - The overturning stability equals a root finder: Given storey forces 100, 200 and 300 kN at 3.5, 7.0 and 10.5 m, a weight of 1 MN, a base of 4 m and a tie-down moment of 0.1 MN m When M_ov is the dot product and the base width that balances the moments is found with brentq Then M_ov, M_stab, the required base width 9.6 m and the required tie-down moment equal the Rust values
  - The accelerogram spectra equal a state space simulation: Given deterministic integer derived records of 200 samples at 0.02 s When the 5 % damped pseudo-acceleration at T = 0.1 s, 0.5 s and 1.0 s and at 2 % damping is simulated with scipy.signal.lsim and first-order-hold input Then the Rust exact recursion agrees to 1e-9 and the set judgement (mean zero-period acceleration, lowest mean ratio, its period and the common scale factor) equals the numpy values
  - The elastic spectrum surface equals the closed forms of EN 1998-1 3.2.2.2: Given a_gR = 0.6 m/s2, S = 1.2 and the corner periods 0.15 s, 0.5 s and 2.0 s When S_e(T, xi) is evaluated for xi = 2, 5 and 30 % with eta = max(sqrt(10 / (5 + xi)), 0.55) Then the grid ordinates of the Rust surface equal the closed forms
  - The diaphragm, overturning and accelerogram checks fail with remedies that fix them: Given a thin diaphragm, a narrow base and scaled-down records When the checks are evaluated and every remedy is applied with a margin of 0.1 % Then the shear, chord, overturning, zero-period and spectrum checks pass, a dangling storey or building reference fails the integrity check and fewer than three usable records fail the count check
  - The new constants are unverified registry rows: Given the stabilising factor, the zero-period ratio and the transfer factor When the checks cite them Then every row stays unverified and is listed in the check
  - Variable actions are patched per keyed element: Given a storey, a bridge or a tower with variable actions When a variable action is inserted, removed or changed Then the diff holds one removal, insertion or modification entry of the keyed variables lane and no whole list
  - A bridge on piers and bearings equals a finite element model: Given a 40 m deck on two piers and four bearings with pier stiffness 3EI/H^3 in series with the bearings When the deck beam is assembled from Hermite elements with lumped masses and solved with scipy.linalg.eigh and the support forces are combined by CQC Then the rigid-deck period, the transverse periods, the effective modal masses, the support forces, the displacements and the seat length equal the Rust values from the mechanics kernel
  - The bridge action rules equal plain arithmetic: Given a bridge of importance class III, a vertical spectrum at four periods, piers of shear span ratio 1, 2 and 5, three seismic components and a cracked inertia share of 0.5 When gamma_I, the vertical spectrum, the behaviour factor q = 3.5 lambda(alpha_s), the component combination and the pier stiffness are evaluated with itertools and plain arithmetic Then gamma_I, S_ve, q, the largest permutation of E_x + 0.3 E_y + 0.3 E_z and the cracked stiffness equal the Rust values, a squat pier below alpha_s = 1 has no behaviour factor and the importance class, the shear span and the component combination checks fail with remedies that fix them
  - The computed pier stiffness equals the concreteproperties moment-curvature: Given a pier 0.8 by 1.2 m with a longitudinal reinforcement ratio of 0.008, a cover of 0.08 m, f_ck 30 MPa, f_yk 500 MPa and an axial load of 0 and 1 MN on the computed stiffness basis When EI_eff = M_y/phi_y is taken from the shared fibre section kernel and the same section is analysed with concreteproperties and the first yield of the tension steel is searched on its moment-curvature curve Then phi_y, M_y and EI_eff equal the library values within 1.5 percent, compression stiffens the section and the declared and the computed pier of one bridge enter the support stiffness 3 EI/H^3 with their own share while a computed section without reinforcement leaves the pier without stiffness and the stiffness check fails with a remedy on the reinforcement ratio
  - The wall pressure of a tank equals the Bessel series: Given a tank of 9 m fluid height and 5 m radius When the impulsive series and the first sloshing mode are evaluated with scipy.special and integrated with quad Then the pressures, the wall resultants, the Housner masses within their tolerance, the sloshing wave and the hoop stress equal the Rust values
  - A tower on a rotational foundation spring equals the frequency determinant: Given a cantilever with a base spring of 1e10 N m per rad When the roots of the 3 by 3 determinant are found with brentq and the same discretisation is solved with scipy.linalg.eigh Then the periods, the effective modal masses, the participation factors and the period lengthening equal the Rust values from the mechanics kernel
  - The bridge, tank and tower checks fail with remedies that fix them: Given a weak pier, bearing, shell, filling ratio, overturning resistance and foundation stiffness When the checks are evaluated and every remedy is applied with a margin of 0.1 % Then the flexure, shear, displacement, seat, pressure and interaction checks no longer fail and the constants they cite stay unverified registry rows
  - The tie force of a foundation tie beam is the registry coefficient times alpha S and the larger supported weight: Given the committed EN 1998 document check-outcome seismic-tie-slope-pass with ground type B (coefficient 0.3), a_g gamma_I = 0.72 m/s2, S = 1.25 and a tie steel of 12 cm2 at 434.8 MPa When the tie beam is checked Then N = 0.3 alpha S N_Ed equals the independent numpy value `en1998.5.tie-beam` of the blessed oracle case within the numerical-v1 profile And the utilisation N / (A_s f_yd) equals the Python oracle `🔮️oracles/🚦️check-outcome` And ground types without a registered coefficient report not applicable
  - The seismic slope factor is the least Bishop factor of the given and of the critical circle: Given the same document with F_H = 0.5 alpha S S_T W, F_V = ±0.33 F_H or ±0.5 F_H and the M2 strengths When the factor is computed by the shared mechanics slope kernel and by the sliced circle solved with scipy brentq on a grid of centres and radii Then F_static, F_given, F_critical and F_s of the blessed oracle case `en1998.5.seismic-slope` agree within the numerical-v1 profile And the utilisation 1 / F_s equals the Python oracle within 1e-5
